{"stories":[{"slug":"judar-pasha","title":"Judar Pasha: The Slave Boy Who Marched Across the Sahara","hook":"Born in Spain. Enslaved as a boy. Then he led an army across the Sahara.","summary":"In 1590 a Moroccan sultan sent thousands of men and animals across the world's largest hot desert to attack the Songhai Empire. The man he chose to lead them was a eunuch born in Spain.","url":"/stories/judar-pasha/","thumb":"/assets/img/thumbs/stories/judar-pasha.jpg","status":"published","era":"1590s","place":"Morocco & Mali","continent":"africa","countries":["mar","mli","esp"],"countryNames":["Morocco","Mali","Spain"],"categories":["military","africa","lost-worlds"],"catNames":["Military","African History","Empires & Lost Worlds"],"keywords":["Morocco","Mali","Songhai","Timbuktu","Gao","Tondibi","Sahara","Ahmad al-Mansur","Spain","Almeria","eunuch","invasion","1591"],"video":false},{"slug":"joyita","title":"The Joyita: Found Adrift With No One Aboard","hook":"25 people sailed. The ship came back without them.","summary":"In 1955 the Joyita left Samoa on a two-day voyage. Thirty-seven days later she was found drifting near Fiji, still afloat – and every one of the 25 people aboard was gone.","url":"/stories/joyita/","thumb":"/assets/img/thumbs/stories/joyita.jpg","status":"published","era":"1955","place":"Pacific Ocean","continent":"oceania","countries":["wsm","fji","nzl"],"countryNames":["Samoa","Fiji","New Zealand"],"categories":["mysteries","strange"],"catNames":["Mysteries","Strange but True"],"keywords":["ghost ship","Samoa","Fiji","Tokelau","Apia","Vanua Levu","Pacific","missing","disappearance","1955","sea mystery"],"video":true},{"slug":"psalmanazar","title":"George Psalmanazar: The Man From Nowhere","hook":"He told London he came from a faraway island. For years, people believed him.","summary":"In the early 1700s a Frenchman claimed to be the first native of Formosa – today's Taiwan – ever to visit Europe. Many in Britain believed him, until he was revealed to be 